Subject: [PATCH 06842/11362] Sharpen O2: which winner has the best EBM
 opportunity -> forge, ported in

Operator follow-up: "which of the top 3 projects have the best potential
improvement opportunity using energy based models... I am looking for a
way to embrace and extend the live agent solving hidden games." Answer:
forge, specifically because it's the only one of the three winners with
an EXPLICIT external candidate-generation-then-selection seam (Duck
reasons/searches internally in one Python-writing turn; Reki emits one
plan per call -- neither has a clean external hook without a control-flow
redesign). Operator decision on the follow-up question (fork vs port):
port into our own E3AgentPolicy stack, not fork forge's codebase --
we already have search-graph/RESET-replay/reproduction-gate
infrastructure none of the three winners have.

Reading our own code before finalizing the task (python/carnot/agentic/
arc_competition_agent.py) found the original O2 framing was wrong: we are
NOT missing forge's arbiter slot, we already have a richer version of it
(candidate_router: cross_game_discriminative_v3_tiebreaker + a
DAgger-trained value head + goal_energy_candidate_guidance_enabled +
world_model_dsl_wired), AND the codebase already defines the exact
bare-control toggle forge's own ablation used (bare_control_config,
candidate_router: None). What's actually missing is the measurement: a
search of results/*.json found no dedicated experiment running forge's
own ablation methodology (matched budget, full stack vs bare control,
report the delta) against our own stack -- so the "our scorer is the
arbiter forge wanted but couldn't afford" claim is architecturally
plausible but currently unverified.

Updated docs/research-notes/arc-agi3-milestone1-winners-sota-ingestion-
2026-07-11.md's O2 section with the corrected, code-grounded plan, and
added ops/known-issues.md active ARC priority list task 12 (the controlled
A/B experiment) plus an operator_override clearing the exclusion-manifest
scope-match guard (new measurement work, not a rerun of any prior
attempt).

